# Line endings — one rule, both directions. Applied to this repo before it ships
# to anyone, because `aiteam init` will tell every consuming project to write this
# exact line (07_portability.md §5) and a framework that trips its own gate on a
# fresh Windows clone has no standing to ask.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its *system* config, which says
# "the working tree should be CRLF". Files written by a tool that bypasses git's
# smudge filter — an editor, a Python script — land as LF, and git then reports
# them as modified forever with an empty diff. Attributes override core.autocrlf
# on every machine, so pinning eol here fixes it for good and travels with the
# repo instead of living in one box's config.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
